
 NZEUS Deck - Debian 12 "bookworm" on the R36S console (modern kernel)

 Where things are:
   /            this system: the file nzeus/nzroot.img on the SD card.
                It becomes writable only after a file system check at start-up.
   /data        your NZEUS files: the file nzeus/nzdata.img. Kept when you
                install a newer NZEUS - put everything you care about here.
   /sdcard      the SD card itself (your games, cubegm/, nzeus/). Read-write.
                Don't touch cubegm/ or nzeus/*.img: the console starts from them.
   /tmp         RAM, only 8 MB. No big files there.

 Useful commands:
   nzeus-status            kernel, memory, battery, card, USB
   poweroff                switch off cleanly (or hold the power button 3 s)
   wifi-up / wifi-down     Wi-Fi with a USB dongle (settings: /data/nzeus/wifi.conf)
   apt update; apt install NAME     more programs (needs Wi-Fi)

 To go back to the console's own system: put the card in a Windows PC and run
 uninstall.bat from the NZEUS download.

